-module(libsodium_crypto_aead_aegis256).
-moduledoc """
AEGIS-256 authenticated encryption with additional data. AEGIS is very
fast on CPUs with AES instructions (libsodium falls back to a portable
implementation elsewhere) and produces `abytes/0` (32) byte tags.

Keys are `keybytes/0` (32) bytes and nonces `npubbytes/0` (32) bytes. The
nonce is long enough to be generated at random for every message (for
example with `libsodium_randombytes:buf/1`) without practical risk of
collision, though a nonce must still never be reused with the same key.

```erlang
Key = libsodium_crypto_aead_aegis256:keygen(),
Nonce = libsodium_randombytes:buf(libsodium_crypto_aead_aegis256:npubbytes()),
Ciphertext = libsodium_crypto_aead_aegis256:encrypt(<<"message">>, <<"header">>, Nonce, Key),
<<"message">> = libsodium_crypto_aead_aegis256:decrypt(Ciphertext, <<"header">>, Nonce, Key).
```
""".
-moduledoc #{author => ["Andrew Bennett <potatosaladx@gmail.com>"]}.
-moduledoc #{created => "2015-12-28", modified => "2026-10-26"}.
-moduledoc #{copyright => "Andrew Bennett"}.
